{
  "series": "series5-recovery-glm53",
  "purpose": "V2 recovery comparison: three calibration episodes and the gate, then three task instances (blocks) each run under four arms after the same persistent scripted fault (false card at cycle 4, repeated once after release): Q quarantine and restrict only, C quarantine and cull without replacement, R0 cull and replace with the ordinary brief and normal graph access, RG cull and replace with the minimal verified packet. Preregistered primary outcome: audited useful post-intervention work by the deadline, RG minus R0 within block; secondary: final audited correct, chosen_is_best, cycles from sanction to final, replacement productivity, cost. Episode is the unit, block is the stratum; nothing is retried or pooled across versions.",
